Policies: Agent

Purpose:
  Defines agent execution policies including risk classification,
  approval requirements, stop conditions, and quality gates.
  This is the single source of truth for all policy decisions.

RiskLevels:
  R0:
    safe: Read file, list files, search
  R1:
    low: Create temp file, run formatter, run unit test
  R2:
    moderate: Modify source, install dependency, change config
  R3:
    high: DB migration, change security config, infra change
  R4:
    critical: Production deployment, secret rotation, data migration
  R5:
    destructive: Delete production data, drop database, destroy infra

ApprovalMatrix:
  R0:
    AUTO
  R1:
    AUTO
  R2:
    AUTO / POLICY
  R3:
    APPROVAL
  R4:
    APPROVAL
  R5:
    EXPLICIT_APPROVAL

PolicyHierarchy:
  Global:
    Applies to all projects
  Project:
    Applies to current project
  Action:
    Applies to specific action

ConflictResolution:
  Most specific policy wins.
  When in conflict, safer policy wins.

StopConditions:
  SECURITY_CRITICAL:
    Stop immediately
  POLICY_VIOLATION:
    Stop immediately
  CONTEXT_INSUFFICIENT:
    Stop and request more context
  UNSAFE_COMMAND:
    Stop and report
  PRODUCTION_RISK:
    Stop and request approval
  DATA_LOSS_RISK:
    Stop and request approval
  TEST_FAILURE:
    Stop and report
  UNEXPECTED_DIFF:
    Stop and review

StopActions:
  STOP:
    Halt execution
  REPORT:
    Report to user
  WAIT:
    Wait for human input

QualityGates:
  BUILD:
    PASS / FAIL
  TEST:
    PASS / FAIL
  BDD:
    PASS / FAIL
  SECURITY:
    PASS / FAIL
  LINT:
    PASS / FAIL
  TYPECHECK:
    PASS / FAIL

  All gates MUST pass before marking task READY.

BDDFirstEnforcement:
  If project policy requires BDD:
    Agent MUST create BDD scenario before implementation.

EscalationRules:
  [AP1]  After 3 failed attempts, agent MUST escalate to human.
  [AP2]  Production actions ALWAYS require explicit approval.
  [AP3]  Agent MUST NOT auto-approve actions with data loss risk.
  [AP4]  Agent MUST record approval decision in audit log.

PolicyRules:
  [PL1]  Policy hierarchy: Global → Project → Action.
  [PL2]  Most specific policy wins.
  [PL3]  When in conflict, safer policy wins.
  [PL4]  Agent MUST stop on any stop condition.
  [PL5]  All quality gates MUST pass before task completion.
  [PL6]  BDD-first enforcement when project policy requires it.

State: +